{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/kernel at 567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a on request/kernel-cache-orchestration.\n\nThe unified history cache is unchanged. This head adds only the narrow repair in internal/gitstore, and the kernel artifact moves with it because the exact head moved.\n\nOne kernel-side decision is worth recording rather than leaving implicit. TestVerifierRejectsCommitTreeDifferentFromSignedPayloadTree names the deleted method, and the request allowed removing its method-specific test. I checked what it does before touching it: it builds a commit over a substituted tree and asserts Verify rejects it with commit tree differs from signed intent. It never called Store.CommitTree, and the invariant it guards is still enforced — now through the metadata tree rather than a separate read. Deleting it would have removed the only assertion that the new tree source is still checked against the signed intent, which is precisely the failure I raised against the CI deduplication earlier: a guard removed because the thing it named had moved. It stays.\n\nThe predecessor at this path is not retired here. Codex recorded it, and decideSupersede admits a supersession only from the target's own author or an actor holding ratifier, with no exemption for naming a successor. So this path carries two live artifacts until codex retires its own; the request covering that is filed with the review request.","body":{"branch":"request/kernel-cache-orchestration","commit":"567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a","head":"567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a","path":"internal/kernel"}}